:" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/biconnectedComponents()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/biconnectedComponents()","abstract":[{"text":"The biconnected components, or blocks (Boost’s, NetworkX’s and igraph’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"biconnected_components"},{"text":"): the maximal biconnected subgraphs, as sets of edges, which they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"partition (self-loops apart: a self-loop is in no block). Blocks are ordered by their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest edge position, each listing its edges in ascending position. An isolated vertex,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or one with only self-loops, is in no block. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"title":"biconnectedComponents()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"biconnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity21BiconnectedComponentsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/biconnectedcomponents()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/bridges()":{"title":"bridges()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/br